# Vercel Sandbox's settings (`metacomputer vm create NAME --on vercel` writes them to config/vms/NAME.env), as comments:
# nothing here is read as a setting; config/defaults.env has the defaults every computer shares. Its docs: docs/vercel.md.
#   PLACE=vercel, PROVIDER=vercel, TRANSPORT=vercel
#   VERCEL_SANDBOX           the sandbox (the computer's name by default; vm create --sandbox)
#   SIZE                     2x4 (the default), 4x8 or 8x16: vCPUs x GB (Hobby allows 4x8 at most); fixed when it's made
#   REGION                   one of Vercel Sandbox's regions; none: the project's default (iad1 unless set). Fixed when
#                            it's made (its snapshots stay in their region)
#   IDLE_STOP                minutes a session runs on after its last use (15 by default; off: until the plan's cap)
#   EGRESS                   internet or off: Vercel's network policy, outside the computer (net allow lists names)
# Its credentials, in the environment of the commands that need Vercel (from your secrets manager, for that command):
#   VERCEL_TOKEN             an access token of the team (team-wide: docs/vercel.md)
#   VERCEL_TEAM_ID           the team (team_...)
#   VERCEL_PROJECT_ID        the project its sandboxes are made in (prj_...)
# They reach lib/remote.py and the computer's broker (providers/vercel/broker.py) only.
